WEBVTT

1
00:00:18.247 --> 00:00:19.008
Maggie cried.

2
00:00:19.028 --> 00:00:20.829
"Do you think that's the van?"

3
00:00:21.750 --> 00:00:23.711
Henry looked up from tying his shoelace.

4
00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:29.776
His cousin, Maggie, was jumping up and down and pointing down the street.

5
00:00:30.664 --> 00:00:34.726
"William said that his parents were sending a blue van to pick us up," Henry said.

6
00:00:34.746 --> 00:00:36.567
"That must be the one."

7
00:00:37.447 --> 00:00:39.448
Cole grabbed his backpack off the sidewalk.

8
00:00:39.468 --> 00:00:42.049
"I can't wait to get to the beach!"

9
00:00:42.469 --> 00:00:43.169
he exclaimed.

10
00:00:43.189 --> 00:00:45.990
"Me neither," Henry agreed.

11
00:00:46.831 --> 00:00:51.153
Their new friend, William, had invited the three of them to spend the weekend at his family's beach

12
00:00:51.193 --> 00:00:56.895
house. It was on an island located about an hour's drive from Belltown, where they all lived.

13
00:00:58.075 --> 00:00:59.396
The van stopped at the curb.

14
00:01:00.968 --> 00:01:02.189
A young woman was driving.

15
00:01:02.209 --> 00:01:04.651
"Are you Henry, Maggie, and Cole?"

16
00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:06.432
she asked in a friendly voice.

17
00:01:06.452 --> 00:01:08.153
"That's them!"

18
00:01:08.533 --> 00:01:10.275
someone called out from the back of the van.

19
00:01:10.295 --> 00:01:12.096
"Get in here, you guys!"

20
00:01:12.957 --> 00:01:15.118
A second later the side door slid open.

21
00:01:15.138 --> 00:01:18.340
"Hi, Nathan," Henry said to the kid inside.

22
00:01:19.181 --> 00:01:23.384
Nathan lived nearby and was one of the friendliest and happiest kids Henry knew.

23
00:01:24.264 --> 00:01:26.346
He was going to William's vacation house too.

24
00:01:26.366 --> 00:01:28.948
"This is going to be great!"

25
00:01:29.292 --> 00:01:31.173
Cole said as he climbed into the van.

26
00:01:31.994 --> 00:01:33.215
Maggie climbed in after him.

27
00:01:33.235 --> 00:01:35.216
"Yeah," she agreed.

28
00:01:35.236 --> 00:01:41.841
"But I wish I didn't have to close the lemonade stand for the whole weekend."

29
00:01:42.722 --> 00:01:43.542
Cole made a face.

30
00:01:43.562 --> 00:01:45.083
"Are you kidding?"

31
00:01:45.464 --> 00:01:45.904
he said.

32
00:01:45.924 --> 00:01:50.567
"I'd much rather spend the weekend at the beach than pouring lemonade."

33
00:01:50.587 --> 00:01:53.329
"Me too," Maggie said.

34
00:01:53.349 --> 00:01:57.032
"But I could make a lot of money selling lemonade this weekend.

35
00:01:57.876 --> 00:01:59.176
And I'm saving up right now.

36
00:02:00.057 --> 00:02:04.038
My barn is having a horse show at the end of the summer, and it costs a lot

37
00:02:04.078 --> 00:02:05.098
to compete in the show."

38
00:02:05.118 --> 00:02:08.659
"You should have plenty of money for that," Cole said.

39
00:02:08.679 --> 00:02:11.780
"Our detective business has been booming lately.

40
00:02:12.620 --> 00:02:16.001
We solved the mystery of the missing baseball glove for Tiny last week."

41
00:02:16.881 --> 00:02:17.621
Henry nodded.

42
00:02:17.641 --> 00:02:19.442
"And we helped Mr.

43
00:02:19.502 --> 00:02:23.223
Metz find his relatives' addresses so he could plan a family reunion.

44
00:02:24.063 --> 00:02:27.264
He paid us double our usual fee for that, remember?"

45
00:02:28.328 --> 00:02:29.309
"I guess you're right."

46
00:02:31.050 --> 00:02:35.292
Maggie stared out the window, still thinking about the lemonade stand as the van pulled away.

47
00:02:35.312 --> 00:02:37.834
"Anyway, we'll be back on Monday.

48
00:02:38.714 --> 00:02:41.636
I hope everybody in Belltown is still thirsty when we get back."

49
00:02:42.516 --> 00:02:44.818
Cole shrugged and then turned to Nathan and Henry.

50
00:02:44.838 --> 00:02:48.400
"Do you think we'll get to go surfing at William's beach house?"

51
00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:49.361
he wondered.

52
00:02:49.381 --> 00:02:52.142
"I don't know," Nathan said.

53
00:02:52.162 --> 00:02:55.024
"I talked to William on the phone yesterday.

54
00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:58.501
But I didn't get to ask him many questions about this weekend.

55
00:02:59.282 --> 00:03:00.602
He sounded kind of weird."

56
00:03:01.462 --> 00:03:02.603
"He sounded weird?"

57
00:03:02.943 --> 00:03:03.583
Henry said.

58
00:03:03.603 --> 00:03:05.064
"What do you mean?"

59
00:03:05.084 --> 00:03:07.685
"He was quieter than usual."

60
00:03:08.225 --> 00:03:09.226
Nathan looked worried.

61
00:03:09.246 --> 00:03:11.267
"I hope he's not getting sick."

62
00:03:11.287 --> 00:03:14.208
"Was he coughing and sneezing on the phone?"

63
00:03:14.648 --> 00:03:15.368
asked Cole.

64
00:03:16.269 --> 00:03:21.271
"No. But my sister Nora has a really bad cold right now," Nathan said.

65
00:03:21.291 --> 00:03:23.712
"I guess that's what made me think of it."

66
00:03:24.532 --> 00:03:27.654
"Let's talk about all the fun stuff we're going to do at the beach!"

67
00:03:28.074 --> 00:03:29.775
Maggie said, changing the subject.

68
00:03:29.795 --> 00:03:32.216
"Yeah," Cole agreed.

69
00:03:32.236 --> 00:03:39.200
"Like swimming and bodysurfing "Maybe we can do pirate things," Nathan suggested.

70
00:03:39.220 --> 00:03:41.061
"Pirates are cool!"

71
00:03:41.081 --> 00:03:45.124
"I want to build a sand castle," Maggie said.

72
00:03:45.144 --> 00:03:47.345
"And look for seashells."

73
00:03:48.666 --> 00:03:49.406
Henry grinned.

74
00:03:49.426 --> 00:03:52.608
"I can't wait to do all that stuff!"

75
00:03:56.140 --> 00:03:58.861
"Here we are," the van driver said an hour later.

76
00:03:59.821 --> 00:04:01.081
Henry looked out the window.

77
00:04:01.862 --> 00:04:04.002
They were approaching a large, fancy house.

78
00:04:04.922 --> 00:04:09.144
It sat near a sandy beach and was bigger than Henry's house and Maggie's house put together.

79
00:04:12.124 --> 00:04:15.485
In the distance Henry could see a long row of tall, rocky cliffs.

80
00:04:15.505 --> 00:04:18.406
"Wow, this place is great!"

81
00:04:18.846 --> 00:04:19.766
Maggie exclaimed.

82
00:04:19.786 --> 00:04:22.147
"We're going to have so much fun."

83
00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:24.048
"Look, there's William."

84
00:04:24.428 --> 00:04:25.228
Nathan pointed.

85
00:04:26.152 --> 00:04:27.833
A kid was standing in front of the house.

86
00:04:28.493 --> 00:04:30.233
A girl around his age was beside him.

87
00:04:31.233 --> 00:04:34.514
As soon as the driver stopped the van, Henry and the others jumped out.

88
00:04:34.534 --> 00:04:37.015
"Hi, William," Henry said.

89
00:04:37.035 --> 00:04:38.795
"Thanks for inviting us!"

90
00:04:38.815 --> 00:04:41.376
"You're welcome," William said.

91
00:04:42.196 --> 00:04:43.217
He pointed to the girl.

92
00:04:43.237 --> 00:04:44.717
"This is Anna.

93
00:04:45.237 --> 00:04:46.558
She lives here in Sea Cove."

94
00:04:46.578 --> 00:04:50.118
"You live at the beach all year long?

95
00:04:50.739 --> 00:04:52.599
Cool!" said Cole.

96
00:04:52.619 --> 00:04:53.679
"I'm Cole."

97
00:04:53.699 --> 00:04:56.429
"And I'm Henry," Henry said.

98
00:04:56.449 --> 00:04:59.812
"That's my cousin, Maggie, and that's Nathan."

99
00:04:59.832 --> 00:05:02.714
"Nice to meet you," Anna said.

100
00:05:02.734 --> 00:05:09.981
"Is this your first time coming to—" Suddenly a figure, waving a long, gleaming sword, leaped from behind

101
00:05:10.041 --> 00:05:10.481
a shrub.

102
00:05:10.501 --> 00:05:13.064
"Aargh!" he growled.
